---
import './design-aids.css';
import NormalisationTable from './NormalisationTable.astro';
---
<figure id="schema-fragmentation" class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface fragmentation wide" aria-labelledby="fragmentation-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration · Table boundaries</span>
  <h3 id="fragmentation-title">Three tables do not improve this dependency</h3>
  <p>In both arrangements, product_id determines the name and current price. Splitting those attributes apart does not remove a repeated product fact.</p>
  <div class="alternatives">
    <div>
      <h4>Keep the product facts together</h4>
      <NormalisationTable label="products" columns={['product_id','name','current_price']} rows={[[ 'P7','Blue mug','€20']]} keys={[0]} />
      <div class="fact-fan"><code>P7</code><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span>Blue mug</span><span>€20</span></div></div>
      <p>A name correction changes the name. A price change changes the price. Each is already stored once.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4>Split the same facts across tables</h4>
      <NormalisationTable label="products" columns={['product_id']} rows={[[ 'P7']]} keys={[0]} />
      <div class="split-path"><span aria-hidden="true">↙</span><span>Match P7 in both tables</span><span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></div>
      <div class="fragments">
        <NormalisationTable label="product_names" columns={['product_id','name']} rows={[[ 'P7','Blue mug']]} keys={[0]} />
        <NormalisationTable label="product_prices" columns={['product_id','current_price']} rows={[[ 'P7','€20']]} keys={[0]} />
      </div>
      <p>Rebuilding the same product needs joins. We also need rules for whether every product must have both related records.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>A separate price table could be useful for multiple currencies, price history or a different access boundary. Those requirements would change what its rows mean. With only one current EUR price per product, this split has not solved a normalisation problem.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .fragmentation.wide { margin-left:50%; }
  .alternatives { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1.2fr); gap:2rem; margin-top:1.5rem; }
  .alternatives > div { min-width:0; }
  .alternatives > div + div { border-left:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); padding-left:1.5rem; }
  .alternatives p { font-size:.82rem; }
  .fragments { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap:1rem; }
  .split-path { display:flex; justify-content:space-around; gap:.5rem; align-items:center; margin:.7rem 0; color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.75rem; }
  .split-path > span[aria-hidden] { color:var(--teal); font-size:1.8rem; }
  .fact-fan { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; gap:1.5rem; margin:2rem 0; }
  .fact-fan > span { color:var(--teal); font-size:2rem; }
  .fact-fan > div { display:grid; gap:1rem; border-left:2px solid var(--teal); padding-left:1rem; }
  @media(max-width:800px) { .alternatives { grid-template-columns:1fr; } .alternatives > div + div { border-left:0; border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); padding:1.5rem 0 0; } }
  @media(max-width:450px) { .fragments { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
</style>
